<title>SINGAPORE: UOB renames unit, boosts paid-up capital.</title>
<headline>UOB renames unit, boosts paid-up capital.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Overseas Bank Ltd (UOB) said on Friday its wholly-owned merchant banking subsidiary, United IBV Ltd, has been renamed UOB Asia Ltd (UOBA) from January 8, 1997.</p>
<p>A bank statement said UOBA, which is based in Hong Kong, has also increased its paid-up capital to HK$75 million, after a rights issue in December.</p>
<p>UOBA is expected to play a more active role in investment management, corporate finance, advisory services and underwriting in North Asia, the statement added.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
